        <article class="article" aria-label="REA getting started guide">
          <section class="article-section" id="computer">
            <h2>1. Prepare your computer</h2>
            <p>
              Use the computer where your target files are stored. A local
              coding agent can read those files and run tools for you.
            </p>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="open-terminal">
              <summary>How do I open a terminal?</summary>
              <ul>
                <li>
                  <strong>Windows:</strong> open the Start menu, type
                  <em>PowerShell</em> and press Enter.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>macOS:</strong> press <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>Space</kbd>,
                  type <em>Terminal</em> and press Enter.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>Linux:</strong> press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <kbd>Alt</kbd>
                  <kbd>T</kbd> on most desktops.
                </li>
              </ul>
              <p>
                Paste a command with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <kbd>V</kbd> (macOS:
                <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>V</kbd>; Linux terminals: <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>
                <kbd>Shift</kbd> <kbd>V</kbd>), then press Enter.
              </p>
              <p>
                Commands go in the terminal. Prompts labeled “Your coding agent”
                go in the agent's chat.
              </p>
            </details>
            <p class="requirements">
              You'll need <span translate="no">Node.js</span> 22 (22.19+), 24
              (24.11+) or 26+. npm comes with
              <span translate="no">Node.js</span>.
            </p>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="install-node">
              <summary>
                Don't have <span translate="no">Node.js</span>, or not sure?
              </summary>
              <p>Open a terminal and check:</p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span>Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="node-check"
                    aria-label="Copy Node.js version check"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="node-check">node -v
npm -v</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                If <code>node -v</code> prints v22.19+, v24.11+ or v26+, you're
                ready. If it prints an older version or "not recognized" /
                "command not found", install
                <span translate="no">Node.js</span> 24 LTS:
              </p>
              <details class="evidence-details" id="node-windows-help">
                <summary translate="no">Windows (PowerShell)</summary>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="code-header">
                    <span>Windows PowerShell</span
                    ><button
                      class="copy-button"
                      type="button"
                      data-copy="node-windows"
                      aria-label="Copy Node.js installation command for Windows"
                    >
                      Copy
                    </button>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code id="node-windows">winget install --exact --id OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS</code></pre>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Type Y if asked to accept the terms. Close PowerShell, open it
                  again, then run <code>node -v</code>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/download"
                    >Download the Node.js installer</a
                  >
                  if winget is unavailable.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If PowerShell later says
                  <em>"running scripts is disabled on this system"</em> when you
                  run <code>npx</code>, use <code>npx.cmd</code> instead. For
                  npm, use <code>npm.cmd</code>:
                </p>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="code-header">
                    <span>Windows PowerShell</span
                    ><button
                      class="copy-button"
                      type="button"
                      data-copy="node-windows-shim"
                      aria-label="Copy Windows REA setup command"
                    >
                      Copy
                    </button>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code id="node-windows-shim">npx.cmd rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
                </div>
              </details>
              <details class="evidence-details" id="node-macos-help">
                <summary translate="no">macOS</summary>
                <p>
                  For a first installation, download the
                  <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/download"
                    >Node.js 24 LTS macOS installer (.pkg)</a
                  >, open it and follow the installer. Then reopen Terminal.
                </p>
                <details class="evidence-details">
                  <summary>Already use Homebrew?</summary>
                  <div class="code-block">
                    <div class="code-header">
                      <span>macOS · Homebrew</span
                      ><button
                        class="copy-button"
                        type="button"
                        data-copy="node-macos-brew"
                        aria-label="Copy Homebrew Node.js installation command"
                      >
                        Copy
                      </button>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code id="node-macos-brew">brew install node</code></pre>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </details>
              <details class="evidence-details" id="node-linux-help">
                <summary translate="no">Linux</summary>
                <p>
                  Install curl and unzip first if they are missing. On Debian or
                  Ubuntu, run <code>sudo apt install curl unzip</code>; on other
                  distributions, use your package manager.
                </p>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="code-header">
                    <span>Linux</span
                    ><button
                      class="copy-button"
                      type="button"
                      data-copy="node-linux-fnm"
                      aria-label="Copy fnm installation command for Linux"
                    >
                      Copy
                    </button>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code id="node-linux-fnm">curl -fsSL https://fnm.vercel.app/install | bash</code></pre>
                </div>
                <p>Close the terminal, open it again, then:</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="code-header">
                    <span>Linux</span
                    ><button
                      class="copy-button"
                      type="button"
                      data-copy="node-linux-install"
                      aria-label="Copy Node.js 24 commands for Linux"
                    >
                      Copy
                    </button>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code id="node-linux-install">fnm install 24
fnm use 24
fnm default 24</code></pre>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Your distribution's own <code>nodejs</code> package is often
                  older than 22.19, so check <code>node -v</code> if you use it
                  instead.
                </p>
              </details>
              <p>
                Prefer a regular installer? Download the LTS version from
                <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/download">nodejs.org</a>.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="working-folder">
              <summary>Make a working folder for your agent</summary>
              <p>
                In your terminal, make a folder for the exercise, then move into
                it:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="make-work-folder"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="make-work-folder">mkdir rea-work
cd rea-work</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Keep this terminal open for the next step. If you already have a
                working folder, open it instead.
              </p>
            </details>
          </section>
          <section class="article-section" id="choose-agent">
            <h2>2. Choose a coding agent</h2>
            <p>
              Your agent is the AI you talk to. REA supplies the inspection
              tools it uses. Pick one client below; open its instructions if you
              haven't used it before.
            </p>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="client-codex">
              <summary>Codex · use your ChatGPT account</summary>
              <p>Install Codex using the command for your operating system:</p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Windows PowerShell</span>
                  <button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-codex-windows"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-codex-windows">powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1 | iex"</code></pre>
              </div>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">macOS / Linux</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-codex"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-codex">curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                After installation, reopen your terminal and return to the
                working folder. Then start Codex:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="launch-codex"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="launch-codex">codex</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Choose “Sign in with ChatGPT”, complete the browser sign-in,
                then return to the terminal. When the message box appears,
                continue to step 3.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/codex/cli"
                  >Codex installation and sign-in</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="client-editors">
              <summary>Cursor, Windsurf or VS Code · use an editor</summary>
              <ol>
                <li>
                  Install the editor for your operating system and sign in.
                </li>
                <li>Open the rea-work folder you made in step 1.</li>
                <li>
                  Open its AI chat and choose Agent mode. In Windsurf or Devin
                  Desktop, open the agent chat; in VS Code, set up GitHub
                  Copilot first.
                </li>
              </ol>
              <p>
                <a href="https://cursor.com/docs">Cursor setup</a> ·
                <a href="https://docs.windsurf.com/windsurf/getting-started"
                  >Windsurf / Devin Desktop setup</a
                >
                ·
                <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/setup/copilot"
                  >VS Code and Copilot setup</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="client-claude-code">
              <summary>Claude Code · use your Claude account</summary>
              <p>Install using the command for your operating system:</p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Windows PowerShell</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-claude-windows"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-claude-windows">irm https://claude.ai/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>
              </div>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">macOS / Linux</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-claude-unix"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-claude-unix">curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Reopen your terminal, return to your working folder and run
                <code>claude</code>. Follow the sign-in prompts. Access uses an
                eligible Claude subscription or a configured API account.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup"
                  >Claude Code installation and account options</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="client-claude-desktop">
              <summary>Claude Desktop · use a desktop chat</summary>
              <p>
                Install Claude Desktop on Windows or macOS and sign in. Quit it
                completely, then run this command in a terminal you opened
                outside Claude:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span>
                  <button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="setup-claude-desktop"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="setup-claude-desktop">npx rea-agents@latest setup --client claude_desktop</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Review and approve the plan, reopen Claude, then
                <a href="#check-connection">check the connection in step 3</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href="https://claude.ai/download">Download Claude Desktop</a>
                ·
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/client-configuration.md#claude-desktop"
                  >Claude Desktop connection details</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="client-opencode">
              <summary>OpenCode · choose an AI model</summary>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-opencode"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-opencode">npm install --global opencode-ai</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Run <code>opencode</code> in your working folder. Use
                <code>/connect</code> in its chat to connect your model account,
                then select a model.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href="https://opencode.ai/docs/"
                  >OpenCode installation and model setup</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details" id="supported-clients">
              <summary>All supported clients and setup IDs</summary>
              <p>
                The npm 6.4.0 release supports the clients below. Use the ID
