                  >EVM bytecode</a
                >
                · <a href="../guides/">All investigation guides</a>
              </p>
            </details>
          </section>
          <section class="article-section" id="terminal">
            <h2>Use REA from a terminal</h2>
            <details class="evidence-details">
              <summary>CLI commands, global installation and curl</summary>
              <p>
                Analyze a JavaScript or Electron application folder or ASAR
                archive without running the app:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span>Static application analysis</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="terminal-analysis"
                    aria-label="Copy JavaScript analysis command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="terminal-analysis">npx -y rea-agents@latest analyze-javascript-application "/absolute/path/to/app" --json</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Replace the path with your extracted app directory or
                <code>.asar</code> file. On Windows, a path such as
                <code>"D:/apps/example"</code> works here.
              </p>
              <details class="evidence-details">
                <summary>Where do I find an app's .asar file?</summary>
                <p>
                  Electron apps usually keep it in a
                  <code>resources</code> folder:
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    <strong>Windows:</strong>
                    <code
                      >C:\Users\&lt;you&gt;\AppData\Local\Programs\&lt;App&gt;\resources\app.asar</code
                    >
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <strong>macOS:</strong>
                    <code
                      >/Applications/&lt;App&gt;.app/Contents/Resources/app.asar</code
                    >
                    (right-click the app and choose
                    <em>Show Package Contents</em>)
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <strong>Linux:</strong> often
                    <code>/opt/&lt;App&gt;/resources/app.asar</code>
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  Some apps install elsewhere. Search the app's folder for
                  <code>app.asar</code>.
                </p>
              </details>
              <p>
                The result identifies the app, shows connections between modules
                and gives their source locations. Connections REA cannot resolve
                are marked in the result.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you'd like a permanent <code>rea</code> command in your
                shell:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span>Install the CLI</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-cli"
                    aria-label="Copy CLI installation command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-cli">npm install --global rea-agents</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                <a href="../guides/javascript/"
                  >Continue with the JavaScript application guide</a
                >
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="native-function"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="native-function">npx -y rea-agents@latest function "/absolute/path/to/program" main --provider ghidra --json</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Replace <code>main</code> with a function name or address from
                the target's function list. Ghidra must be configured first.
              </p>
              <p id="curl-installation">
                On macOS or Linux, you can also use the curl installer after
                preparing Node.js:
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">macOS / Linux</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="install-curl"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="install-curl">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/morluto/rea/main/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                Follow the setup prompts to connect your agent. If they don't
                appear, run <code>rea setup</code>.
              </p>
              <p id="curl-setup-path">
                If your shell can't find <code>rea</code>, use the executable
                path printed by the installer. On Linux, the default setup
                command is <code>"$HOME/.local/bin/rea" setup</code>.
              </p>
            </details>
          </section>
          <section class="article-section" id="help">
            <h2>Getting help</h2>
            <details class="evidence-details">
              <summary>If your agent doesn't see REA</summary>
              <p>
                Restart or reconnect the client after setup. Check its REA
                connection with <code>doctor</code>; for Codex:
              </p>
              <p>
                Use the client check in step 3 with your setup ID. In editor
                clients, enable REA in MCP settings and allow its tools in the
                agent chat.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details">
              <summary>If a provider needs attention</summary>
              <p>Check the provider you're using. For Ghidra:</p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span>Check one provider</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="provider-doctor"
                    aria-label="Copy provider diagnosis command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="provider-doctor">npx -y rea-agents@latest doctor --provider ghidra --json</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                The report gives the failed check and a suggested next step.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details">
              <summary>Windows, WSL and paths with spaces</summary>
              <p>
                Use Windows PowerShell for Windows clients and analysis tools.
                If your agent runs inside WSL, install Node.js and REA inside
                that Linux environment and use Linux paths there. Headless
                providers run on the same host as REA.
              </p>
              <p>
                In a terminal, put quotes around a path that contains spaces.
              </p>
              <p>Windows setup command:</p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Windows PowerShell</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="windows-setup-command"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="windows-setup-command">npx.cmd rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="evidence-details">
              <summary>Update or remove REA</summary>
              <p>
                To refresh your agent connection, run the latest setup command
                again, review its plan and restart your client.
              </p>
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-header">
                  <span translate="no">Terminal</span
                  ><button
                    class="copy-button"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy="refresh-rea"
                    aria-label="Copy command"
                  >
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre><code id="refresh-rea">npx rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
              </div>
              <p>
                If you installed the global CLI, update it with
                <code>rea update</code>. Use
                <code>npx rea-agents@latest uninstall</code> to remove REA's
                client configuration and skill.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md#diagnose-update-and-remove"
                  >Update and uninstall details</a
                >
              </p>
            </details>
            <ul class="reading-list">
              <li>
                <a href="../faq/">REA FAQ</a
                ><span>Quick answers on updates, agents and analysis.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="../guides/">Choose an investigation guide</a
                ><span
                  >Worked examples for a binary, an Electron app and a
                  browser.</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues">GitHub issues</a
                ><span>Report a problem with the command and diagnostics.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://discord.gg/GkcryMnJDM">REA community</a
                ><span>Questions, investigations and work in progress.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </article>
