      <div class="page-heading">
        <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="../">Home</a> / Showcases</p>
        <h1>REA case studies.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Android, games, Electron and a CTF challenge, with code, figures and
          checked results.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-index">
        <section class="guide-entry">
          <p class="eyebrow">Android · APK analysis</p>
          <div>
            <h2>How an authenticator generates a login code</h2>
            <p>
              Find Aegis's six-digit code calculation in its released APK. Trace
              the generating methods with REA, then move a demo clock to see why
              the code changes every 30 seconds.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-route">
              <span>APK</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Generating code</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Recovered rule</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Adjustable clock</span>
            </div>
            <a class="text-link" href="aegis/">Read the Android case study</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="guide-entry">
          <p class="eyebrow">CTF · Native analysis</p>
          <div>
            <h2>Solve a CTF flag checker</h2>
            <p>
              Inspect an easy DownUnderCTF challenge with REA. Find its checking
              functions, turn masks and sums into equations, then verify the
              solved flag with the original program.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-route">
              <span>Binary</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Checking code</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Equations</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Correct!</span>
            </div>
            <a class="text-link" href="ctf/">Read the CTF case study</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="guide-entry">
          <p class="eyebrow">Native · Reconstruction</p>
          <div>
            <h2>DX-Ball's sound-pan calculation</h2>
            <p>
              Recover a sound-pan calculation from a 1996 Windows game. REA's
              instructions, caller references and numeric constants lead to a
              small C function, checked against the original behavior and all 63
              compiled bytes.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-route">
              <span>Executable</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>REA findings</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Recovered C</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Validation</span>
            </div>
            <a class="text-link" href="dx-ball/">Read the DX-Ball case study</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="guide-entry">
          <p class="eyebrow">Electron · Feature tracing</p>
          <div>
            <h2>How Notion copies text and HTML</h2>
            <p>
              Trace a page-facing API through Notion's packaged JavaScript.
              Follow its IPC wrappers to the system clipboard, then see how a
              small HTML marker keeps rich block data connected to a copy.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-route">
              <span>Packaged app</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Exposed API</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>IPC wrappers</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Clipboard</span>
            </div>
            <a class="text-link" href="notion/">Read the Notion case study</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="guide-entry">
          <p class="eyebrow">PC-98 DOS · Reconstruction</p>
          <div>
            <h2>How TH04 aims a ring of bullets</h2>
            <p>
              Inspect the original 16-bit angle helper with REA. Match its
              multiply, divide and coordinate operations to readable C++, then
              see how they produce a ring aimed at the player.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-route">
              <span>Original DOS code</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>REA instructions</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Angle calculation</span> <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
              <span>Bullet ring</span>
            </div>
            <a class="text-link" href="th04/">Read the TH04 case study</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Step-by-step guides</h2>
        <p>
          The guides walk through a native calculation, an Electron export and a
          browser request. Each starts with a prompt and a concrete target.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="../guides/">Read the guides</a>
      </section>
