      <section class="section" id="what-is-re">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="lede">
            Reverse engineering means learning how software works by inspecting
            the program itself. With REA, your agent can follow the code,
            explain a feature and help you rebuild it.
          </p>
          <ol class="home-workflow" id="how-rea-helps">
            <li>
              <h3>Ask about one feature</h3>
              <p>Give your agent a program or page and a question.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Inspect the program</h3>
              <p>REA returns code, references and runtime observations.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Explain it, then try a change</h3>
              <p>
                Your agent uses the findings to explain or rebuild the feature.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <details class="home-evidence-details">
            <summary>See the full Calculator investigation</summary>
            <p class="comparison-question">
              Why does Calculator give 220 for
              <span translate="no">200 + 10%</span>?
            </p>
            <figure class="home-role-comparison">
              <div
                class="manual-investigation step-comparison"
                data-step-comparison
              >
                <h3 class="comparison-label">
                  Follow the instructions step by step
                </h3>
                <div
                  class="step-selector expert-step-selector"
                  role="group"
                  aria-label="Follow the manual Calculator analysis"
                >
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    data-select-step="1"
                    aria-pressed="true"
                    aria-controls="expert-assembly expert-reasoning"
                  >
                    <span>01</span> Decode branches
                  </button>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    data-select-step="2"
                    aria-pressed="false"
                    aria-controls="expert-assembly expert-reasoning"
                  >
                    <span>02</span> Trace calls
                  </button>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    data-select-step="3"
                    aria-pressed="false"
                    aria-controls="expert-assembly expert-reasoning"
                  >
                    <span>03</span> Recover the rule
                  </button>
                </div>
                <div class="expert-analysis-grid">
                  <details class="code-block expert-assembly" open>
                    <summary class="code-header">
                      <span>Original x64 · selected instructions</span>
                      <span
                        class="assembly-disclosure"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                      ></span>
                    </summary>
                    <pre><code id="expert-assembly"><span class="code-step is-active" data-step="1">0x180124945: MOV EAX, dword ptr [R13 + 0x18]
0x180124949: CMP EAX, 0x5c
0x18012494c: JZ 0x180124aba
0x180124952: CMP EAX, 0x5b
0x180124955: JZ 0x180124aba</span>
<span class="code-step" data-step="2">0x18012495b: MOV EDX, 0x64
0x180124960: LEA RCX, [RSP + 0x160]
0x180124968: CALL 0x180122650
0x18012496e: LEA RDX, [R13 + 0x160]
0x180124975: LEA RCX, [RSP + 0x78]
0x18012497a: CALL 0x180109720</span>
0x18012497f: MOV RSI, RAX
0x180124982: MOV qword ptr [RSP + 0x28], RAX
<span class="code-step" data-step="2">0x180124987: LEA RDX, [RSP + 0x160]
0x18012498f: MOV RCX, RAX
0x180124992: CALL 0x180123190</span>
<span class="assembly-omission">; … value-copy instructions omitted …</span>
<span class="code-step" data-step="3">0x180124a14: MOV RDX, RDI
0x180124a17: LEA RCX, [RSP + 0xf8]
0x180124a1f: CALL 0x180109720
0x180124a24: LEA R8, [RSP + 0x30]
0x180124a29: MOV RDX, RAX
0x180124a2c: LEA RCX, [RSP + 0xb8]
0x180124a34: CALL 0x180123c10</span></code></pre>
                  </details>
                  <aside
                    class="expert-reasoning"
                    aria-label="Illustrative expert reasoning"
                  >
                    <div
                      id="expert-reasoning"
                      aria-live="polite"
                      aria-atomic="true"
                    >
                      <div class="expert-thought" data-step-note="1">
                        <p class="thought-label">01 · Which branch?</p>
                        <p>
                          “<strong>0x5b? 0x5c?</strong> Two jumps to the same
                          place. Which operators are these?”
                        </p>
                        <p class="expert-task">
                          Look up the command IDs, then label the branch.
                        </p>
                        <dl class="expert-facts">
                          <div>
                            <dt>0x5b</dt>
                            <dd>Divide ÷</dd>
                          </div>
                          <div>
                            <dt>0x5c</dt>
                            <dd>Multiply ×</dd>
                          </div>
                        </dl>
                      </div>
                      <div class="expert-thought" data-step-note="2">
                        <p class="thought-label">02 · What do the calls do?</p>
                        <p>
                          “100 is clear. The calls are just addresses.
                          <strong
                            >Which one divides? Which value goes in?</strong
                          >”
                        </p>
                        <p class="expert-task">
                          Inspect the helpers and trace the stored values.
                        </p>
                        <dl class="expert-facts">
                          <div>
                            <dt>0x64</dt>
                            <dd>100</dd>
                          </div>
                          <div>
                            <dt>…123190</dt>
                            <dd>Divide</dd>
                          </div>
                        </dl>
                      </div>
                      <div class="expert-thought" data-step-note="3">
                        <p class="thought-label">03 · What is the rule?</p>
                        <p>
                          “This path multiplies by the other input. So
                          <strong>10% means 10% of 200</strong> after +.”
                        </p>
                        <p class="expert-task">
                          Name the operands and check both operator paths.
                        </p>
                        <div class="expert-rule">
                          <span>200 × 10 / 100</span>
                          <strong>20</strong>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <img
                      class="expert-illustration"
                      src="assets/figures/analyst-thinking.svg"
                      alt=""
                      width="160"
                      height="120"
                    />
                    <p class="expert-caption">Illustrative expert reasoning</p>
                  </aside>
                </div>
                <p class="manual-work-summary">
                  <strong
                    >You decode the instructions, follow the calls and
                    reconstruct the calculation.</strong
                  >
                </p>
              </div>
